 Deployment helpers for the internal services.
 
-`bin/notify-deploy.sh SERVICE VERSION` restarts the service on the deploy host and posts a
-message to the release channel. The webhook URL comes from `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` in the
-environment; per-service settings live in `etc/services.conf`.
+`bin/notify-deploy.sh [--dry-run] SERVICE VERSION [NOTE]` restarts the service on the deploy
+host and posts a message to the release channel. The webhook URL comes from
+`SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` in the environment; per-service settings live in `etc/services.conf`.
+
+- `SERVICE` must match `[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*` and `VERSION` must be letters, digits, and `._+-`
+  (up to 64 characters each); anything else is rejected.
+- `NOTE` is an optional short release note (up to 500 characters). It appears in the Slack
+  message on a line after the deploy summary. Quote it so the shell passes it as one argument:
+
+  ```
+  bin/notify-deploy.sh web 1.4.2 "Fixes the login redirect loop"
+  ```
+
+- `--dry-run` prints what the script would do (the `ssh` command and the Slack payload) and
+  exits without restarting the service or posting the message. The webhook URL is never
+  printed; a dry run does not require `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` to be set.
